    "title": "Is Easter Monday a holiday? are banks open? What to know",
    "text": "LOCALIs Easter Monday a holiday? Not in the U.S. Jordan GreenMemphis Commercial AppealApril 6, 2026, 9:47 a.m. CTGlobally, Easter Monday is observed by most countries, but in the United States, its status remains a source of annual confusion.Easter Monday, observed the day after Easter, is recognized by Christians across the globe and is a public holiday in many countries, including Canada, the United Kingdom and much of Europe.In the United States, some schools and employers may choose to close for the day, but it is on an individual case-by-case basis, not a set standard.",
